HST Office: no empty band below the native menu bar (gtk3) once the lazily built menu bar shows.

hst-gtk-menubar-lazy-build.patch builds the native GTK menu bar on an idle. When the window's menu bar is
created, MenuBar::ImplCreate gives the VCL menu bar window height 0 only if the native menu bar is already
visible; with the build pending it is not, so the VCL window keeps its own height (34 px here) and
ImplBorderWindow::GetBorder keeps that much space at the top of the client. The native menu bar then shows
above it, and the VCL window paints nothing under a native menu bar: an unthemed white band between the menu
bar and the content. Every window that shows its menu bar from the start has it; the Start Center always
does (the Tabbed UI hides the menu bar of documents, so their windows do not). Measured on 1.0.2 rc and the
1.0.3 Start Center: the container window's TopInset is 34 and the Start Center 34 px shorter than the window.

GtkSalMenu::BuildPendingMenuBar now lays the VCL menu bar out again after it created the native widget
(MenuBar::LayoutChanged, as EnableUnity does), which gives the VCL window height 0. Nothing else changes: the
idle, the document tab strip (LayoutManager border space) and the notebookbar strip are untouched.

Check: tests/runtime/check-start-center-top-border.py (gtk3): a lone Start Center has TopInset 0 and fills its
window; two documents still show the document tab strip.

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).
---
diff --git a/vcl/unx/gtk3/gtksalmenu.cxx b/vcl/unx/gtk3/gtksalmenu.cxx
index 23d88fa..eb3cabf 100644
--- a/vcl/unx/gtk3/gtksalmenu.cxx
+++ b/vcl/unx/gtk3/gtksalmenu.cxx
@@ -1115,6 +1115,11 @@ void GtkSalMenu::BuildPendingMenuBar()
     {
         DestroyMenuBarWidget();
         CreateMenuBarWidget();
+        // The VCL menubar window kept its own height while the native menubar was pending, and the
+        // window's border kept that much space at the top of the client (an empty band below the
+        // native menubar). Now that the native one shows, the VCL one goes to height 0.
+        if (!pMenuBar->isDisposed())
+            pMenuBar->LayoutChanged();
     }
 }
 
